BUILD 90 - Dagon, Lord of the Poisoned Deep no longer stands frozen

- FIXED: Dagon, Lord of the Poisoned Deep stood frozen in place. He now walks, runs,
  attacks, staggers, dies and casts Tidal Strike, his signature move, with an
  animation of his own for the first time.
- This bug dates all the way back to the original Soulvizier. Dagon was built out of
  the Hydra, and every one of his animation clips was left pointing at the Hydra
  skeleton, which has 101 bones. His actual body is a deep-one mage with 30 bones and
  none of that structure, so not one of those clips could drive it. The animation
  table his record named was a leftover that has never existed in any release of the
  mod or of the base game, so there was no fallback either. He is now bound to his own
  rig, the one the base game uses for 43 of his 44 same-body relatives.
- Also fixed: three of his special-move slots were still labelled with Hydra breath
  attacks, so the game went looking for the wrong animation when he cast. They now
  name the skills he actually uses.
- NEW PERMANENT GATE: every build from here on checks that no monster that can spawn
  ships with an animation chain that resolves from nothing, and that Dagon in
  particular only ever binds clips from a rig his body can play. A monster can no
  longer ship with animations that cannot drive it. The same freeze class already
  took the maenad thrown-weapon fighters in an earlier build.
- Nothing else about Dagon changed: same fight, same skills, same soul, same drop
  chance, same mystical orb.

Database only. No map, quest or text change: your characters, saves and items are
untouched. Fully quit the game and restart Steam to pick up the update.
